IMPORT daydate

-- National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1998-39.txt (legislation.gov.uk,
-- revised text, point in time 7 April 2026).

§ `National Minimum Wage Act 1998 — the nouns`

§§ `The individual and the work (ss 1, 34-45, 54)`

-- s 28(1): in civil proceedings a person is presumed to qualify "unless the
-- contrary is established". The three conditions of s 1(2) are therefore
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN: NOTHING is "not established either way". Each exclusion is
-- a BOOLEAN that is TRUE only when the facts it needs are established.
DECLARE `Qualification facts` HAS
    -- s 54(3): a contract of employment, or a contract to do or perform
    -- personally work or services for a party who is not a client or
    -- customer of the individual's business.
    `has a worker's contract`                           IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    -- s 34(1): supplied by an agent to do work for a principal, with no
    -- worker's contract with either, and not in business on their own
    -- account with the work's recipient as client or customer.
    `an agency worker within s 34`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 35: a home worker (works at a place not under the other party's
    -- control or management, for that party's business), who would be a
    -- worker if "personally" read "(whether personally or otherwise)".
    `a home worker within s 35`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 1(2)(b).
    `working or ordinarily working in the United Kingdom` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    -- s 40: on board a ship registered in the United Kingdom under Part II
    -- of the Merchant Shipping Act 1995.
    `employed on a ship registered in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment is wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ordinarily resident in the United Kingdom`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 1(2)(c).
    `has ceased to be of compulsory school age`         IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(2)(a): prevented from qualifying by regulations under s 3.
    `prevented from qualifying by regulations under s 3` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the kind of work`                                  IS A `Kind of work`
    `voluntary work`                                    IS A `Voluntary work facts`
    `community`                                         IS A `Community facts`

-- The work, where an exclusion turns on what it is.
DECLARE `Kind of work` IS ONE OF
    `ordinary work`
    -- s 37(1): service as a member of the naval, military or air forces of
    -- the Crown (not employment by a Reserve Forces Act association, s 37(2)).
    `service in the armed forces`
    -- s 37A: a member of the Combined Cadet Force, Sea Cadet Corps, Army
    -- Cadet Force or Air Training Corps assisting its activities otherwise
    -- than in the course of Crown employment.
    `assisting a cadet force`
    -- s 43: master or crew of a fishing vessel.
    `on a fishing vessel` HAS
        `remunerated only by a share in the profits or gross earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 45: a prisoner, in pursuance of prison rules.
    `prison work under prison rules`
    -- s 45A: a work order under Schedule 6 to the Courts Act 2003.
    `unpaid work to discharge a fine`
    -- s 45B: Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 s 153A disqualifies the person.
    `work disqualified by s 153A of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999`

-- s 44.
DECLARE `Voluntary work facts` HAS
    `employed by a charity, voluntary organisation, associated fund-raising body or statutory body` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (1)(a): no monetary payments, or none except expenses actually incurred
    -- in the performance of the duties (including (1A) expenses) or
    -- reasonably estimated as likely to be or have been so incurred.
    `receives and is entitled to no money except expenses, apart from any money solely for subsistence` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (2): money paid solely to provide means of subsistence.
    `also receives money solely for subsistence`        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (2)(a)-(b): employed under arrangements made between a charity acting
    -- in pursuance of its charitable purposes and the body the work is
    -- for, which is itself a charity, voluntary organisation, associated
    -- fund-raising body or statutory body.
    `placed by a charity with such a body`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (1)(b), (3): no benefits in kind except subsistence or reasonable
    -- accommodation (training to improve ability to do the work left out).
    `receives and is entitled to no benefits in kind except subsistence or reasonable accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 44A.
DECLARE `Community facts` HAS
    `a residential member of a community employing them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the community is or was established by a charity`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a purpose is to practise or advance a religious or similar belief` IS A BOOLEAN
    `members live together for that purpose`            IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (3): an independent school, an alternative provision Academy that is
    -- not one, or a provider of a course of further or higher education.
    `a school or a provider of further or higher education` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Pay reference periods (s 17)`

DECLARE `Pay reference period` HAS
    -- Worked out under the s 2 regulations.
    `hours of work`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `relevant remuneration received`                    IS A NUMBER
    -- s 17(4) "R1 is the rate of national minimum wage which was payable in
    -- respect of the worker during the pay reference period".
    `rate payable during the period`                    IS A NUMBER
    -- Payments of additional remuneration already made for this period, in
    -- the order made.
    `payments of additional remuneration`               IS A LIST OF `Payment of arrears`

DECLARE `Payment of arrears` HAS
    `amount paid`                                       IS A NUMBER
    -- R2 as it stood when this payment was made: the rate the worker would
    -- have had during the period under the regulations then in force.
    `rate for the period under the regulations then in force` IS A NUMBER

-- A pay reference period with R2 at the time of determination (s 17(4)).
DECLARE `Underpaid period` HAS
    `the period`                                        IS A `Pay reference period`
    `rate for the period at the time of determination`  IS A NUMBER

§§ `Access to records (ss 10, 11, 11A)`

DECLARE `Records request` HAS
    -- s 10(2): the worker believes on reasonable grounds that they are or
    -- may have been paid less than the national minimum wage.
    `believes on reasonable grounds they were underpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10(5): a production notice was given.
    `production notice received on`                     IS A DATE
    -- s 10(9)(b): a later time agreed during the fourteen days.
    `later day agreed for production`                   IS A MAYBE DATE
    -- s 11(1): the records were not produced in accordance with s 10(8)-(9),
    -- or the worker was not allowed to inspect, copy or be accompanied.
    `the employer failed to produce or allow inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 11A: early conciliation.
    `early conciliation`                                IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`
    `complaint presented on`                            IS A DATE
    -- s 11(4): the tribunal is satisfied it was not reasonably practicable
    -- to present it in time, and it came within a further reasonable period.
    `tribunal allows it as presented within a further reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 11(2)(b): "as in force when the award is made".
    `hourly national minimum wage when the award is made` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Early conciliation` HAS
    -- s 11A(1)(a): the worker complies with s 18A(1) of the Employment
    -- Tribunals Act 1996.
    `Day A`                                             IS A DATE
    -- s 11A(1)(b): the worker receives, or is treated as receiving, the
    -- certificate.
    `Day B`                                             IS A DATE
